body:
@mj12albert I noticed release v1.3.0 does this:

> Fix field validation when Form errors or invalid prop are present at same time (#4112) 

However, the current issue still exists.  The `Field.Root`'s `invalid` prop should have precedence. It's presence implies the ability to control it, but in actuality the constraint validation has precedence and is too forceful. If manually setting `invalid` is not the final arbiter, then something like `invalid={null}` should at least be able to reset (i.e., disable) the constraint validation.
